(8, 55, '<p style=\"text-align:center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><strong>AIRPORT SHUTTLE BOOKING FORM</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">To:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Milton<br />\r\nDate:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 6. ##blank##&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;No. of passengers: One</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bus Time:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;7. ##blank## pm&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Type to ticket: Single</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Name:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Janet 8. ##blank##</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Flight No:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;9. ##blank##&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;From: London Heathrow</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Address in Milton:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Vacation Motel 24, Kitchener Street</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fare:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; $35</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Credit Card No: (&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Visa) 10. ##blank##</span></p>', 'no', '[\"17th October\\/17th of October\\/the 17th October\\/the 17th of October\",\"12.30\",\"Thomson\",\"\\u0410\\u0421 936\",\"3303 8450 2045 6837\"]', 5, NULL, NULL),
(9, 13, '<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">In our modern world, one prominent issue that demands our attention is the 11. ##blank## of a throwaway society marked by excessive consumerism. A key reason behind this problem is the concept of planned obsolescence. Many products are intentionally designed with limited lifespans, forcing consumers to replace them more frequently than necessary. This strategy drives sales but significantly contributes to excessive waste. Moreover, pervasive consumer culture and 12. ##blank## pressures encourage people to buy more than they need and frequently discard items that are still functional. The culture of convenience and the rapid turnover of fashion trends have also given rise to disposable clothing and other goods, further 13. ##blank## the throwaway culture. Additionally, the 14. ##blank## of economic growth over environmental sustainability by governments and businesses has led to policies that encourage increased production and 15. ##blank##.</span></p>', 'no', '[\"prevalence\",\"societal\",\"exacerbating\",\"prioritization\",\"consumption\"]', 5, NULL, NULL),
(10, 12, '<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The pie chart provide a 4. ##blank## of the amount of food eaten by two groups of students, while the table highlights some 5. ##blank## of the health. The data suggest that diet may have an impact on levels of absenteeism and on student&rsquo;s ability to stay healthy. The pie charts show that there are 6. ##blank## and differences with regards to the two groups diets. In both group, about a third of the food students eat 7. ##blank## of cereals such as pasta, bread and rice. Similarly, they eat an equal 8. ##blank## of the fish (5 percent). However, the level high-fat food eaten by Group B is 9. ##blank## higher than in Group A, at 50%, while students in Group B eat far fewer vegetables than group A and a slightly smaller amount of fresh fruit. incidence slightly aspects breakdown information similarities requires consists proportion considerably amount coincidence. The table indicates that there are twice as many overweight people in Group B (20 percent) as in Group A. What is more. Group B has experienced a much higher 10. ##blank## of illness over the year, with over double the number of students being absent from classes. This has resulted 15 percent lower attendance rate.</span></p>', 'no', '[\"breakdown\",\"aspects\",\"similarities\",\"consists\",\"proportion\\/amount\",\"considerably\",\"incidence\"]', 7, NULL, NULL),
(11, 33, '<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Unfortunately, if people do not have enough time to relax, there are quite major risks 9. ##blank## with this. Health often suffers, either physically or mentally, and sometimes both. Taking time out for physical leisure activities has positive effects on health through the release of chemicals that make us feel better both physically and mentally. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Friendships can also be weakened because of not making enough time to stay in touch, but using only a little of your free time to have a meal or go to the cinema with someone helps to maintain that friendship. Listening to your friend&#39;s problems, or talking through your own 10. ##blank## your relationship with them, as well as allowing you to switch off mentally from the things that have been happening at work. This &#39;distancing&#39; from work helps you to get things back into perspective and can sometimes help you find solutions to matters that have been 11. ##blank## you. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Within a family situation a partner may feel neglected if the other one spends long hours away at work, or a child may feel neglected because mummy/daddy is never around for birthdays, school performances or a vital sports match. This lack of involvement is a major 12. ##blank## to family breakdown, which in turn has wider 13. ##blank## in our society. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Work is a major part of our lives and it is to be hoped that many find it enjoyable, challenging, and 14. ##blank##, but it is important to 15. ##blank## the need for a work-life balance and to ensure that this is put into practice.</span></p>', 'no', '[\"associated\",\"reinforces\",\"bothering\",\"contribution\",\"repercussions\",\"stimulating\",\"recognize\"]', 7, NULL, NULL),
(12, 32, '<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The number of men obtaining degrees in science from Callum University has 4. ##blank## since 1995, but the trend has not always been 5. ##blank##. Between 1995 and 1997, the university 6. ##blank## a slight increase from just over 4,000 science graduates to just under 5,000. This was followed by a period during which numbers dropped a little and then remained stable. However, between 2000 and 2005, the faculty saw a 7. ##blank## increase in male graduates, and by 2005, their numbers reached a peak of about 7,800, after which they 8. ##blank## back to their current figure of 6,000.</span></p>', 'no', '[\"risen\",\"steady\",\"experienced\",\"dramatic\",\"fell\"]', 5, NULL, NULL),
(13, 51, '<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Rarely is success a linear path and achieving it in life is an intricate 10. ##blank## influenced by a variety of 11. ##blank##. While some individuals contend that attaining success 12. ##blank## mainly on diligence and perseverance, others argue that external factors such as wealth and physical attractiveness play a more significant role. In the following paragraphs, I will explore both perspectives and offer my own 13. ##blank## on this issue. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Those who emphasize the importance of industriousness and persistence in achieving success have a valid point. Hard work is essential because by putting in the time and effort required to master their craft, individuals can improve their performance and achieve higher levels of success. Determination is also 14. ##blank## because it allows individuals to persist in the face of challenges and 15. ##blank##. A clear sense of purpose and direction help individuals stay focused and motivated over the long term. Entrepreneurs like Elon Musk and Jeff Bezos, for instance, have achieved their success through tenacity and dedication, investing long hours and overcoming numerous obstacles along the way.</span></p>', 'no', '[\"endeavor\",\"dynamics\",\"hinges\",\"stance\",\"critical\",\"setbacks\"]', 6, NULL, NULL),
(14, 50, '<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The table gives data about passenger 4. ##blank## reaching a station every 2 hours in a day, and also the average ticket cost at those times. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Passenger numbers 5. ##blank## 3 times during the day. For example, the number at 6am is 480, rising to 690 by 8am before falling again. There is then a peak of 700 at midday, followed by an afternoon 6. ##blank## to a low of 230 at 4pm. A third 7. ##blank## is at 6pm, reaching 670 before tailing off. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The ticket prices partially follow this pattern. The 8am passenger surge is matched by a high price of $29, followed by a peak of $31 at midday and a decrease to $17 by 4pm. However, the 6pm spike in passenger numbers is 8. ##blank## by a low of $11 in prices, with a 9. ##blank## rise to $22 at 8pm and a final levelling off. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:18px\">In summary, ticket prices increase broadly in line with passenger traffic, except during the evening rush hour when they actually fall.</span></p>', 'no', '[\"volumes\",\"peak\",\"decline\",\"spike\",\"accompanied\",\"subsequent\"]', 6, NULL, NULL),
